        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> [@wroyca](https://github.com/wroyca), `setup_termbg_sync()` now uses OSC 111 to by default to reset to terminal's default background. With the option to use previous approach.\n> \n> The main drivers for this change were:\n> \n>     * [`transparency` settings not working when using rose-pine colorscheme with MiniMax inside tmux MiniMax#25](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/issues/25) - `tmux` doesn't quite handle the transparent terminal background.\n> \n>     * `st` [got support for OSC 111](https://git.suckless.org/st/commit/d6c431859c6c0201e0668ed24a9f17cebf0a68f5.html) in its main codebase (not as a patch).\n> \n> \n> I think the latest `main` should work better in the use case described in this issue.\n\n<img width=\"220\" height=\"146\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07f3c81d-7a8a-4f8d-ba24-b1f195afd12c\" />",
